Package: vaultwarden
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd
Section: web
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dani-garcia/vaultwarden
Description: Vaultwarden Password Manager - self-hosted Bitwarden-compatible server
 Vaultwarden is a self-hosted, Bitwarden-compatible password manager
 server written in Rust. It bundles the official web vault (login page
 and admin panel at /admin) and serves the full Bitwarden API, so the
 Bitwarden browser extensions, desktop and mobile apps can connect to
 your NAS directly.
 .
 The app opens in a new browser tab at http://<NAS-IP>:8222 (direct
 port mode: Vaultwarden's API endpoints are hard-mounted at the URL
 root and cannot be served behind a path prefix). A random
 ADMIN_TOKEN is generated at install time; see
 /usr/local/vaultwarden/vaultwarden.env. Vault data (SQLite database,
 attachments, sends, icon cache) lives in /var/lib/vaultwarden and
 survives removal ('apt remove'); 'apt purge' deletes it entirely.
 .
 Note: the browser web vault requires HTTPS to unlock/log in (browser
 WebCrypto secure-context restriction, inherent to all Bitwarden web
 vaults). On plain-HTTP LANs use the Bitwarden clients, or enable
 HTTPS on the NAS / place a reverse proxy in front.
